WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:08.180
This is a quick tutorial on some handy track
display settings in our graphical viewers.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:13.219
You may know that we embed the viewer into
many resources at NCBI, so whether you start

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:18.930
in a Gene record, the Genome Data Viewer,
or in one of our other sequence viewers, these

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.310
settings can be key to your analyses.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.800
Today I'll start in the Gene record for human
CSK.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.119
In the section called, Genomic regions, transcripts,
and products, you'll see the embedded sequence

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:33.230
viewer.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:38.110
If you wanted, you could pop this viewer out
into it's own tab or window using this helix

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.130
icon menu.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:45.830
You will likely see the Genes track in this
configuration, where transcript and CDS pairs

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:51.140
are merged on a single line, and there is
no gene bar; we'll see what a gene bar is

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.390
shortly.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.540
I'll zoom in to this region where the coding
sequence is, and

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:02.050
the first feature that I'll point out is a
new addition to the tooltip information.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:07.340
Mouse over one of the merged rows, and you
get a tooltip showing the total CDS length

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.850
for this transcript and the total Protein
length.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:16.560
Below that are the mRNA and Protein positions
that reflect the position of your cursor when

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.579
you triggered the tooltip.

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:23.579
You will not see this position, or the sequence
information, if you trigger the tooltip when

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:25.210
zoomed out too far.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:30.609
Now let's say you want to see all of the RefSeq
transcripts and proteins annotated for this

00:01:30.609 --> 00:01:31.609
gene.

00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:39.920
You can go into the Tracks, Configure Tracks
menu and change settings there.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.499
But there is a one-step solution.

00:01:42.499 --> 00:01:46.310
Just click on this Show All icon at the top
of the viewer.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:54.009
Now you see the gene bar in green, the purple
mRNA transcripts and the red protein annotations.

00:01:54.009 --> 00:01:57.340
And note that this is a toggle switch.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.210
Here is another short cut for changing the
rendering options.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:07.689
Mouse over the track name, and select the
first icon on the left, the gear icon.

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:13.650
Now you have the same Rendering options menu
we saw in the Tracks, Configure Tracks menu.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:19.000
And you may like this other setting, Product
Features.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:24.190
By selecting �Product Features�, you see
annotated features on the protein product,

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:31.110
such as phosphorylation sites, and domains

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:36.220
As you saw, a mouseover gives you a tooltip
with more information, such as the source

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:41.970
of the feature annotation.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.240
That's it for now.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.110
Here is a summary of the settings I just covered.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:49.290
- the addition of CDS and protein lengths
in tooltips

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:55.000
- the Show All shortcut
- the shortcut to track rendering options

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.690
via the gear icon in the track tooltip, and
- Product Features in the rendering options

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.540
menu.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.450
We would love to have your feedback.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:09.790
You can use the link in the Help menu
or send that feedback and any questions you

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:21.290
may have about any NCBI products via our Support
Center, or by writing to, info@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:27.290
We'll be adding more tidbits in short demos
like this, so stay tuned to the NCBINLM YouTube

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:33.840
channel, including the playlists, NCBI Genome
Data Viewer and NCBI Genome Browsers.

